            <ArticleTitle>Some clinical trials get no respect.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>356-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/clc.20613</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is something to be learned from every randomized clinical trial. However, because of physician bias and/or misinterpretation by the cardiovascular community and by the lay press, some trials seem to generate a lot of heat before they generate light. This is particularly true for trials comparing medical therapy to revascularization, (eg, PCI/stent or coronary artery bypass surgery).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
